codemap 9
tour feature-comments
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note The agent, at the start of a session in which the human says to address their codemap comments (the CLAUDE.md contract of every mapped repo names this loop). Goal: the agent writes the map as a side effect of writing the code, so the questions the human left on the map must reach it. diff, notes and tour read only .codemap/, and comments are deliberately kept out of it (feature-add-comment), so without this command the agent has no way to see a comment at all, short of finding the store inside .jj/repo or the git common dir and parsing its files. It prints one block per open comment: the id, open or answered, who wrote it, its place resolved against the current code (a step's number, index and file:lines; a file:lines and symbol; or what is gone: tour, step, symbol, lines or file), and the text; then how many are open and the exact comment-reply line to answer with. --all adds the answered ones with their replies. The CLI scenarios 'comments' and 'stale' show it before and after replies and after the code under a comment changes, moves or is deleted. Why comments exist and the designs that were tried are in feature-add-comment.

